le at  the damn step Stones no less I'm more  inclined to think this is coreless we  can make out a white-haired woman to the  right possibly his wife rhaenis  correction since I started editing this  video I noticed the windowed designs  here match those found in the king's  chamber where he is dead so unless  they're the same Design This is likely  viserys now I also wonder if viseris  will die a natural death or if someone  will give him a little push the book  offers two scenarios one in which the  king went for a nap and died in his  sleep and the other where Allison gives  the king some poison if anyone were to  give the king some poison I'd argue it  would be rainis as revenge for stealing  her crown here appears to be a maester  or surgeon preparing some surgical tools  when we find renice in front of dozens  of candles whenever I think of many  candles in Game of Thrones I think of  religion so maybe she's praying to some  sort of God or the gods for her  husband's recovery someone who may not  be praying for corliss's Recovery is his  brother vehmond these two have fought a  lot and vaman knows that Luke who's  expected to be Lord of driftmark isn't a  true Valerian so it would make sense  with Corliss potentially on his deathbed  for vaman to come and claim driftmark as  his own we'll later see him questioning  renice who sits on the Driftwood Throne  asking who will sit on it when Corliss  is gone it looks as though training  continues at King's Landing where sir  Kristen abashes Eamonn shield with a  Morning Star just like he did to Damon  in episode 1 overlooking the ominous in  Grim King's Landing we have voice over  of a feeble voiced viserys stating the  crown cannot remain strong if the house  of the Dragon is divided the man is  still holding on to hope that Allison  and radera can patch things up and heal  the rift between their families here we  have Jason Luke watching someone come  through the front Gates of the red keep  someone will later find is abayment  vaman's arrival will undoubtedly cause  more problems for many of our characters  especially if he starts questioning  these strong boy's legitimacy to the  throne when it pertains to driftmark  here we have Damon clutching a piping  hot dragon egg but for whom could this  egg be for maybe his daughter Reina who  had vegar snatch from her or perhaps one  of the three children he'll eventually  have with rhaenyra I'm curious if this  egg is discovered at the dragon pit or  on Dragonstone this looks like Jace to  me visibly upset and with aegon to his  right I wouldn't be surprised if he was  the cause of this anger a cloaked figure  of approaching massaria aka the White  Worm the last we saw of her she ratted  on Damon to Otto Hightower about his  secret died out with rhaenyra as far as  we know Damon does not know it was her  who did this the cloak here suggests  that this is Damon could he be going  back to her to cheat or perhaps asking  for a favor she is well connected with  spies after all it also looks like  Masari is doing quite well for herself  neatly dressed and in an upscale home a  far cry from the prostitute she was in  episode 1. rhaenyra tells Damon here  that this is a trap by going to King's  Landing there's definitely the potential  for lots of traps here's Luke looking a  little concerned followed by eamond  pointing his sword saying nephews of  course referring to Jason Luke if  Episode 7 was Kitty brawl here we have  teen brawl Jace punches Eamon but we can  also see Luke and aegon here and even a  glimpse of Helena in the background  aegon pushes Luke into the table and  just check out the face of who I think  is Reina beside him the preview ends  with Auto telling whomever is in the  king's seat at the small Council likely  Alison that the threat of War looms  because the next shot is of Raymond's  rival in King's Landing it implies that  this may be where the threat comes from  however I wouldn't be surprised if this  threat o